  "id": "ms-mass-hypertrophy-8week",
  "programVersion": "1",
  "name": "8 Week Mass Building Hypertrophy Workout",
  "weeks": 8,
  "daysPerWeek": 4,
  "description": "Four weekly sessions with changing per-set reps, final-set rest-pause, drop sets and slow negatives.",
  "goals": [
    "muscle"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "equipment": [
    "barbell",
    "bench",
    "bodyweight",
    "cable",
    "dumbbells",
    "machine"
  ],
  "schedule": "Suggested week: Monday Chest and Side Delts; Tuesday Upper Back and Rear Delts; Wednesday off; Thursday Arms and Abs; Friday Legs; weekend off. Repeat eight weeks. Other days are allowed; take a day off after at most three consecutive training days, preferably two.",
  "progression": "Choose loads that allow the printed reps; no fixed increment is supplied. Author reply to Clint Morse (9 Jun 2026): repeat each week, aiming for more reps or weight than the previous week.",
  "notes": "For intermediate/advanced trainees. Session duration and warm-up counts are not supplied; duration is left unspecified. Rest 90s between sets and exercises. Symbols apply to the final set only: * rest-pause, + drop set, ^ 3–5s negatives. The prose describes five-second negatives; table keys are retained. Extra mini-sets stay in exercise notes, not fabricated extra target sets. Optional moderate cardio: 20 min, 3–4 times/week, morning or after weights; not inserted as strength days. Unilateral rep counts remain as printed. Walking lunge and calf press follow the linked dumbbell-walking and leg-press-calf guides.",
